# Testing Rules

Testing is first-class, not an afterthought.

- New behavior should normally include automated tests in the same change.
- Every bug fix should include a regression test when reasonably possible.
- `npm test` must run the project's normal automated test suite.

## Determinism & isolation

- Tests must be deterministic — no flaky timing, randomness, or ordering
  dependence.
- Unit tests must not make real network requests.
- Automated tests must **never** call the real OpenAI API.
- Automated tests must **never** send a real SMS message.
- External systems (OpenAI, Twilio) must be replaceable with fakes, mocks,
  or test implementations — this is a direct consequence of the AI
  provider abstraction and transport boundaries in the architecture rule.

## What to test

- Prefer testing behavior and contracts (inputs/outputs, HTTP status codes,
  what the Cookie Man service does with a given AI response) over internal
  implementation details.
- Do not weaken or delete tests just to make them pass — fix the underlying
  issue instead.
